{title: At Calvary}
{artist: William R. Newell / Daniel B. Towner}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: C}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Years I spent in [F]vanity and [C]pride
[C]Caring not my [F]Lord was cruci[C]fied
[C]Knowing not it [F]was for me He [G7]died
On Cal[C]vary
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Mercy there was [F]great, and grace was [C]free
[C]Pardon there was [F]multiplied to [C]me
[C]There my burdened [F]soul found lib[G7]erty
At Cal[C]vary
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]By God's Word at [F]last my sin I [C]learned
[C]Then I trembled [F]at the law I'd [C]spurned
[C]Till my guilty [F]soul imploring [G7]turned
To Cal[C]vary
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Now I've given [F]to Jesus every[C]thing
[C]Now I gladly [F]own Him as my [C]King
[C]Now my raptured [F]soul can only [G7]sing
Of Cal[C]vary
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Oh, the love that [F]drew salvation's [C]plan
[C]Oh, the grace that [F]brought it down to [C]man
[C]Oh, the mighty [F]gulf that God did [G7]span
At Cal[C]vary
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
